# Gemini Chatbot Implementation Plan

This plan outlines the architecture and steps to build a robust chatbot using the `google-genai` SDK, FastAPI for the backend, and Streamlit for the frontend.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> You will need a Google Gemini API Key. You can get one from [Google AI Studio](https://aistudio.google.com/).
> We will store it in a `.env` file in the `backend/` directory.

## Proposed Changes

### Project Structure

We will adopt a modular structure to separate concerns:

```text
chat-bot/
├── backend/
│   ├── app/
│   │   ├── main.py          # FastAPI application & endpoints
│   │   ├── agent.py         # Gemini AI logic (google-genai integration)
│   │   ├── schemas.py       # Pydantic models (request/response)
│   │   └── utils.py         # Helper functions for logging/formatting
│   ├── .env                 # Gemini API Key (keep this private)
│   └── requirements.txt     # Backend dependencies
├── frontend/
│   ├── app.py               # Streamlit UI
│   └── requirements.txt     # Frontend dependencies
└── .gitignore               # Ensure .env and venv are ignored
```

---

### Backend Components

#### [MODIFY] [agent.py](file:///c:/Users/TOMATO651/Desktop/important/work/chat-bot/backend/app/agent.py)
Implement the `GeminiAgent` class using `google-genai`.
- Initialize the client with API key.
- Implement a method for sending messages and receiving responses.
- Support for chat history (multi-turn conversations).

#### [NEW] [schemas.py](file:///c:/Users/TOMATO651/Desktop/important/work/chat-bot/backend/app/schemas.py)
Define `ChatRequest` and `ChatResponse` models.

#### [MODIFY] [main.py](file:///c:/Users/TOMATO651/Desktop/important/work/chat-bot/backend/app/main.py)
Add a POST `/chat` endpoint that:
- Accepts a message and conversation ID.
- Calls [agent.py](file:///c:/Users/TOMATO651/Desktop/important/work/chat-bot/backend/app/agent.py) to get a response.
- Returns the AI's response.

#### [MODIFY] [requirements.txt](file:///c:/Users/TOMATO651/Desktop/important/work/chat-bot/backend/requirements.txt)
Add `google-genai`.

---

### Frontend Components

#### [MODIFY] [app.py](file:///c:/Users/TOMATO651/Desktop/important/work/chat-bot/frontend/app.py)
Build a sleek Streamlit interface:
- Use `st.chat_message` for a modern look.
- Maintain session state for history.
- Connect to the FastAPI backend.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run `pytest` if added (later stage).
- Scripted API test: Use `curl` or a Python script to send a POST request to `/chat` and verify the JSON response.

### Manual Verification
1. Start the FastAPI server: `uvicorn app.main:app --reload`
2. Start the Streamlit app: `streamlit run frontend/app.py`
3. Send a message "Hello" and verify Gemini responds correctly.
4. Test multi-turn behavior: Ask "What is my name?" and verify Gemini remembers if told previously.
5. Check `.env` is properly loaded and not committed to git.
